From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bootowser <b@o.local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 09:12:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [Bootowser] rename the browser to bootowser

Patches 0001 and 0002 decide what the kiosk may do; this one decides
what it calls itself. Everything user-visible that says Firefox now
says Bootowser: the window title, the about dialog, the app menu,
the default browser check, --version.

The identity is split across three places, and it is worth being
explicit about why each one lives where it does:

  * --with-app-name=bootowser, in mozconfig-bootowser, renames the
    executable. That option is MOZ_APP_NAME, which is a plain option
    and so can be set from a mozconfig.

  * MOZ_APP_VENDOR, MOZ_APP_PROFILE and MOZ_APP_UA_NAME cannot be.
    They are project_flags, and configure rejects a mozconfig that
    tries with "can not be set by mozconfig. Values are accepted
    from: implied". Hence the imply_options below.

  * The brand strings themselves are branding data, not build
    configuration, so they are edited where they live rather than
    overridden: browser/branding/unofficial is the directory this
    build actually uses, because browser/confvars.sh points
    MOZ_BRANDING_DIRECTORY at it and nothing passes --with-branding.

The one deliberate exception is the User Agent, which stays
Firefox/<version>. MOZ_APP_UA_NAME defaults to empty, and an empty
one makes nsHttpHandler fall back to application.ini's "Name", so
without pinning it every page would be served "bootowser/156.0" and
the sites a kiosk exists to display would be free to treat it as a
bot. The HTTP-facing identity is not part of the rebrand.

The two update URLs pointed at nightly.mozilla.org. Updates are
disabled by policy and there is no Bootowser update service, so they
now resolve to about:blank: nothing in the build should be able to
reach a Mozilla endpoint even if a policy stops being applied.

MOZ_APP_ID is left at Firefox's GUID. It keys the crash reporter
submission URL and the update channel, both of which still point at
Mozilla infrastructure; a fresh GUID would only orphan them.
---
 browser/branding/unofficial/configure.sh      |  2 +-
 .../unofficial/locales/en-US/brand.ftl        | 12 +++++------
 .../unofficial/locales/en-US/brand.properties |  6 +++---
 .../unofficial/pref/firefox-branding.js       |  4 ++--
 browser/moz.configure                         | 21 ++++++++++++++++++-
 5 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/browser/branding/unofficial/configure.sh b/browser/branding/unofficial/configure.sh
index f42e11ddad..a10dfbda84 100644
--- a/browser/branding/unofficial/configure.sh
+++ b/browser/branding/unofficial/configure.sh
@@ -2,5 +2,5 @@
 # License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
 # file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
 
-MOZ_APP_DISPLAYNAME=Nightly
+MOZ_APP_DISPLAYNAME=Bootowser
 MOZ_MACBUNDLE_ID=nightlyunofficial
diff --git a/browser/branding/unofficial/locales/en-US/brand.ftl b/browser/branding/unofficial/locales/en-US/brand.ftl
index 5eaea9a7c4..1ba13d0424 100644
--- a/browser/branding/unofficial/locales/en-US/brand.ftl
+++ b/browser/branding/unofficial/locales/en-US/brand.ftl
@@ -16,12 +16,12 @@
 ## For further details, consult:
 ## https://mozilla-l10n.github.io/styleguides/mozilla_general/#brands-copyright-and-trademark
 
--brand-shorter-name = Nightly
--brand-short-name = Nightly
--brand-shortcut-name = Nightly
--brand-full-name = Nightly
+-brand-shorter-name = Bootowser
+-brand-short-name = Bootowser
+-brand-shortcut-name = Bootowser
+-brand-full-name = Bootowser
 # This brand name can be used in messages where the product name needs to
 # remain unchanged across different versions (Nightly, Beta, etc.).
--brand-product-name = Firefox
--vendor-short-name = Mozilla
+-brand-product-name = Bootowser
+-vendor-short-name = Bootowser
 trademarkInfo = { " " }
diff --git a/browser/branding/unofficial/locales/en-US/brand.properties b/browser/branding/unofficial/locales/en-US/brand.properties
index 346c3bdb50..c2d4560f3c 100644
--- a/browser/branding/unofficial/locales/en-US/brand.properties
+++ b/browser/branding/unofficial/locales/en-US/brand.properties
@@ -2,6 +2,6 @@
 # License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
 # file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
 
-brandShorterName=Nightly
-brandShortName=Nightly
-brandFullName=Nightly
+brandShorterName=Bootowser
+brandShortName=Bootowser
+brandFullName=Bootowser
diff --git a/browser/branding/unofficial/pref/firefox-branding.js b/browser/branding/unofficial/pref/firefox-branding.js
index f22dd0a51c..cc26a15c9b 100644
--- a/browser/branding/unofficial/pref/firefox-branding.js
+++ b/browser/branding/unofficial/pref/firefox-branding.js
@@ -13,10 +13,10 @@ pref("app.update.interval", 86400); // 24 hours
 pref("app.update.promptWaitTime", 86400);
 // URL user can browse to manually if for some reason all update installation
 // attempts fail.
-pref("app.update.url.manual", "https://nightly.mozilla.org");
+pref("app.update.url.manual", "about:blank");
 // A default value for the "More information about this update" link
 // supplied in the "An update is available" page of the update wizard.
-pref("app.update.url.details", "https://nightly.mozilla.org");
+pref("app.update.url.details", "about:blank");
 
 // The number of days a binary is permitted to be old
 // without checking for an update.  This assumes that
diff --git a/browser/moz.configure b/browser/moz.configure
index 446e8637d0..ed6110e929 100644
--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -11,7 +11,26 @@ imply_option("MOZ_NORMANDY", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_PROFILE_MIGRATOR", True)
 
 
-imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Mozilla")
+# Bootowser identity. These three are project_flags, which configure only
+# accepts from an imply_option -- a mozconfig `export` is rejected outright
+# ("can not be set by mozconfig. Values are accepted from: implied"), so the
+# rebrand has to live here rather than in mozconfig-bootowser.
+#
+# MOZ_APP_UA_NAME is deliberately Firefox and must stay that way unless you also
+# accept that pages gate on it: it defaults to empty, which makes the User
+# Agent fall back to application.ini's "Name", so leaving it out would serve
+# every page "bootowser/<version>" and get the kiosk treated as a bot.
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Bootowser")
+# application.ini's "Profile" field: the profile name inside the profile root.
+# The root itself is not this -- MOZ_DEDICATED_PROFILES is on in browser/, so a
+# build with MOZ_APP_NAME=bootowser profiles under ~/.bootowser/ rather than
+# sharing ~/.mozilla/ with whatever else is installed.
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_PROFILE", "bootowser")
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_UA_NAME", "Firefox")
+# Left as Firefox's GUID on purpose: it keys the crash reporter submission URL
+# and the update channel, which still point at Mozilla infrastructure. Give
+# Bootowser its own GUID only once you also run your own crash collection and a
+# signed update channel.
 imply_option("MOZ_APP_ID", "{ec8030f7-c20a-464f-9b0e-13a3a9e97384}")
 # Include the DevTools client, not just the server (which is the default)
 imply_option("MOZ_DEVTOOLS", "all")
